    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0112" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/10–649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Butler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-06T15:00:00-05:00">October 6, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:22 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. In reply to my question, Hevia<anchor n="81" xml:id="d110-f1"/> told me
                    yesterday Cuba will follow lead of US in its relations with China. He said no
                    question of Cuba’s recognizing Chinese Communist government at present time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d110-f1" n="81" xml:id="d110-f1-content">
                <p>Carlos Hevia, Cuban Minister of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
